# Infra-TAK FeatureLink Display Configurator — component-level ignores.
#
# This file did not previously exist (audit Appendix E §2.1); the Python artefacts of a
# Flask module were caught only by the root file's blanket rules, which is fragile — a
# contributor tightening a root rule would silently un-ignore build output here.
#
# Everything the root .gitignore already covers (OS junk, editor state, logs, .env) is NOT
# repeated here. Only genuine component deltas belong in this file.

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# ── Lint / test / type-check caches ──────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# ── Flask / runtime instance state ───────────────────────────────────────────
instance/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ── Install-script backups ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# install.sh rewrites the console's app.py in place; the remediated version writes a
# timestamped backup beside each file it patches. Those backups are host state, not source.
*.featurelink-backup
*.featurelink-backup.*

# ── NOT ignored, deliberately ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# featurelink_displayconfig_assets/icons/ is 7,461 tracked files that this component ships.
# See docs/remediation/wp5-crosscutting.md for the deduplication proposal — it is a real
# ~7 MB duplication of TAKPortal/assets/featurelink-configurator/icons/, but it must stay
# tracked until a shared corpus exists, or the component stops working.
